Attribution required from downstream users
------------------------------------------

When reusing this dataset, retain the following notice:

  Contains information from EUR-Lex, © European Union, 1998-2026,
  licensed under CC BY 4.0. Structured, identified and diffed by
  EUCITE. Modified from the original.

Every node in the dataset additionally carries its own machine-readable
provenance block (source work, CELEX identifier, source URL, retrieval
timestamp and checksums), so attribution can be reconstructed per node rather
than only per dataset.


Indication of modifications
---------------------------

CC BY 4.0 requires that changes be indicated. This project makes the following
modifications to the upstream material:

  - the text is segmented into a typed node tree;
  - identifiers are attached to each node — inherited from the source where the
    source provides them, derived by this project's parser below the paragraph
    level (each node declares which of the two applies);
  - whitespace and presentation markup are normalised into a canonical form;
  - amendment markers are extracted into structured fields;
  - text from several source works is composed into a single corpus.

No word of the normative text is altered, added or removed.


